    "body": "A string is wrapped around a hockey puck (disk) of mass M = 4 kg and radius R = 0.20 m that sits on a frictionless horizontal ice surface. The figure shows the view from the top. Starting from rest you pull the string with a constant force of magnitude F = 120 N along a horizontal frictionless surface. At the instant when the center of the puck has mvoed a distance d = 0.1 m, a length L = 0.9 m of string has unwound from the disk.\n\n\\textbf{At this instant, what is the angular speed} $\\omega$ \\textbf{of the disk about its center of mass?}\n\nMoment of inertia of the disk is I = (1/2)MR$^2$",
